## Add Chart Repo
```bash
helm repo add homeylab https://homeylab.github.io/helm-charts/
# update the chart, this can also be run to pull new versions of the chart for upgrades
helm repo update homeylab
```

## Prerequisites
Point the exporter at a reachable BookStack instance via `config.host` (e.g. `https://bookstack.example.org`) - **required**.

Authentication uses a BookStack API token, provided one of two ways:

- **Chart-managed Secret** - set `auth.tokenId` / `auth.tokenSecret`. The chart stores them in its own `Secret` and injects them as the `BOOKSTACK_TOKEN_ID` / `BOOKSTACK_TOKEN_SECRET` env vars. Simplest for `helm install --set` or a values file.
- **Bring your own Secret** - set `existingSecret.name` (the chart references it via `secretKeyRef` and creates no Secret of its own). Keys default to `BOOKSTACK_TOKEN_ID` / `BOOKSTACK_TOKEN_SECRET`; override with `existingSecret.tokenIdKey` / `existingSecret.tokenSecretKey`. Good for GitOps / External Secrets Operator.

Either way the tokens are injected as environment variables and are **never written into the chart's `ConfigMap`** (a ConfigMap is not a Secret). Those env vars also override any `credentials` set in `config.yml`.

## Install
```bash
helm install bookstack-file-exporter homeylab/bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter --create-namespace

# with own values file - recommended
helm install -f my-values.yaml bookstack-file-exporter homeylab/bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter --create-namespace
```

### OCI Registry Support
```bash
helm install bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter oci://registry-1.docker.io/homeylabcharts/bookstack-file-exporter --version X.Y.Z --create-namespace

# with own values file - recommended
helm install -f my-values.yaml bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter oci://registry-1.docker.io/homeylabcharts/bookstack-file-exporter --version X.Y.Z --create-namespace
```

### Install Example
Only some options are shown, view `values.yaml` for an exhaustive list.

<details closed>
<summary>custom-values.yaml</summary>
<br>

```yaml
# custom-values.yaml
# API token -> chart-managed Secret -> injected as BOOKSTACK_TOKEN_ID/SECRET env (kept out of the ConfigMap).
# For GitOps/ESO, omit these and set existingSecret.name instead.
auth:
  tokenId: "my-token-id"
  tokenSecret: "my-token-secret"

config:
  host: "https://bookstack.example.org"
  formats:
    - markdown
    - html
  # assets/* are snake_case and pass through 1:1 to upstream config.yml (see Advanced Configuration)
  assets:
    export_images: true
    export_attachments: true
    export_meta: true
  keep_last: 5
  # also upload each backup to an S3 / S3-compatible target; the key material comes from a Secret, not here
  object_storage:
    - name: primary
      endpoint: "minio.example.org"   # leave unset to use AWS S3's default endpoint
      region: "us-east-1"
      bucket: "bookstack-bkps"
      prefix: "bookstack/file_backups/"
      keep_last: 30
      access_key_env: "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID"
      secret_key_env: "AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"

# inject the object_storage keys (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY) from a Secret you manage
# yourself - e.g. one synced by External Secrets Operator - instead of putting them in config
extraEnvFrom:
  - secretRef:
      name: bookstack-file-exporter-s3

persistence:
  enabled: true
  size: 5Gi
```
</details>
<br>

## Scheduling
Set by `config.run_interval`:

- **CronJob (default)** - `config.run_interval: 0` renders a k8s `CronJob` on `cron.schedule` (default `@daily`).
- **Deployment** - `config.run_interval: <seconds>` renders a `Deployment` that loops in-pod, sleeping that long between runs.

> **Note** - upstream's app-native `config.run_schedule` is disabled: the chart fails the render if it's set. Use the k8s `CronJob` or the `run_interval` loop instead.

## Remote Storage
In addition to (or instead of) the local `persistence` volume, the exporter can upload backups to one or more S3 / S3-compatible targets via `config.object_storage` (a list, empty by default). Each entry requires `name`, `endpoint`, `region`, and `bucket`; leave `endpoint` unset to use AWS S3's default endpoint, or set it to point at an S3-compatible provider (e.g. MinIO).

Prefer `access_key_env` / `secret_key_env` (paired with a Secret injected via `extraEnvFrom`, so the actual key material lives in a Secret) or `ambient_auth` (e.g. an IRSA/workload-identity role) for credentials. Setting `access_key` / `secret_key` inline works, but renders them into the chart's `ConfigMap` **in cleartext** - a ConfigMap is not a Secret - so it's discouraged for anything but local testing.

> **Note** - `existingSecret` is token-only (it wires the BookStack API token via `secretKeyRef`). Object-storage key material belongs in a **separate** Secret injected with `extraEnvFrom` (below), so those keys reach the container as env vars matching `access_key_env` / `secret_key_env`.

```yaml
config:
  object_storage:
    - name: primary
      endpoint: "s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com" # leave unset to use AWS S3's default endpoint
      region: "us-east-1"
      bucket: "bookstack-bkps"
      prefix: "bookstack/file_backups/"
      access_key_env: "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID"
      secret_key_env: "AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"

# the S3 key material lives in a Secret you manage (e.g. synced by External Secrets Operator)
extraEnvFrom:
  - secretRef:
      name: my-object-storage-creds
```

## Advanced Configuration
`config.yml` is rendered from `.Values.config`: keys are snake_case, match the [upstream config.yml](https://github.com/homeylab/bookstack-file-exporter/blob/main/docs/configuration.md) 1:1, and empty/default keys are pruned (the exporter rejects `null`/`""`). So any upstream key works even if it isn't in `values.yaml`.

To manage `config.yml` yourself (GitOps, or a key the chart doesn't model), set `config.existingConfigMap` to a ConfigMap with a `config.yml` key - the chart mounts yours and skips rendering its own.

## Upgrade
```bash
helm upgrade bookstack-file-exporter homeylab/bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter

# with own values file - recommended
helm upgrade -f my-values.yaml bookstack-file-exporter homeylab/bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter
```

### OCI Registry Support
```bash
helm upgrade bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter oci://registry-1.docker.io/homeylabcharts/bookstack-file-exporter --version X.Y.Z

# with own values file - recommended
helm upgrade -f my-values.yaml bookstack-file-exporter -n bookstack-file-exporter oci://registry-1.docker.io/homeylabcharts/bookstack-file-exporter --version X.Y.Z
```

### Breaking Changes

| Start Chart Version | Target Chart Version | Upgrade Steps |
| ------------------- | -------------------- | ------------- |
| `1.0.2` | `1.0.3` | Only with `persistence.existingClaim` set: the redundant chart-managed PVC stops rendering, so `helm upgrade` deletes it — and its PersistentVolume and data under the default `Delete` reclaim policy. [Upgrade notes](https://github.com/homeylab/helm-charts/blob/main/charts/bookstack-file-exporter/docs/upgrade.md#from-102-to-103). |
| `0.X.X` | `1.0.0` | Major breaking revision — exporter upgraded to upstream `v3.0.0` (config rewrite, `config` keys now snake_case). **Read the [upgrade notes](https://github.com/homeylab/helm-charts/blob/main/charts/bookstack-file-exporter/docs/upgrade.md#from-0xx-to-100) in full before upgrading.** |

_Upgrades from earlier majors are covered in the [full upgrade notes](https://github.com/homeylab/helm-charts/blob/main/charts/bookstack-file-exporter/docs/upgrade.md)._


